:answer/id #uuid "cd9a3c5b-01ba-58d3-a280-cbf23d6f1ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "330d78e7-780e-5055-bd0b-9c3b943d8801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433981} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8b22932-e413-5c67-a864-5e79c72114a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "78263033-1bff-5da3-9201-fff7488d909f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332828" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-3L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\}=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)=3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}+16} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d856e13-fac1-552c-8875-d611da9c00a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d856e13-fac1-552c-8875-d611da9c00a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433980} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5489e0-fc0c-5c3d-9e36-b3584f966d21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4ba1928-c543-554d-8f81-96f348be498a" :question/math-academy-id "q-333055" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-2\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(1+\\frac{2}{s}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(\\frac{s+2}{s}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-4 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2(-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)})+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{2(s+2)}{s(s-3)}+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)+4s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s-4+4{s}^{2}-12s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b58a5cd-7ca6-5b39-aacf-b77684b7ded0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b58a5cd-7ca6-5b39-aacf-b77684b7ded0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434002} :answer-field/id #uuid "337d0577-b7fc-523e-8b76-50488544ecf7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e326d04-8454-5a4c-8291-8ce0cd1c8852" :question/math-academy-id "q-333061" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3 & =-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+2){X}_{1}(s) & =-3 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{3}{s+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}+1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3(-\\frac{3}{s+2})+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9}{s+2}+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9s}{s(s+2)}+\\frac{(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+5s+{s}^{2}+10+2s}{s(s+2)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7107643e-b101-593c-a4be-aed821d14b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7107643e-b101-593c-a4be-aed821d14b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433999} :answer-field/id #uuid "7711698c-a576-5c6f-98d2-825afa236b73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1151a388-649e-5c91-8e65-af0ed8268c10" :question/math-academy-id "q-333068" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-(\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s(s-2)-(s+5)}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}-2s)-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-4s-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2231d8eb-43c8-5010-a3d6-0228d639d76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2231d8eb-43c8-5010-a3d6-0228d639d76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433977} :answer-field/id #uuid "269c3ef7-1f7e-5b5b-b5b6-94fa2ab0a45d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434034} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d746ceb-03b3-5401-ab18-45b6c0ecc018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d746ceb-03b3-5401-ab18-45b6c0ecc018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434010} :answer-field/id #uuid "df9aae05-0903-5349-afc8-277fbc48692c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "80182570-5c16-548e-a977-c22b33e10f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-333124" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b80eef-df10-542e-9407-86feef4fb7ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{3t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33b80eef-df10-542e-9407-86feef4fb7ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{3t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433982} :answer-field/id #uuid "150cc971-a84f-524e-85be-4ba5c139cbb9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ca7bb14-8c09-5fbf-9824-91b12b83b929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ca7bb14-8c09-5fbf-9824-91b12b83b929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433996} :answer-field/id #uuid "b24e4e2e-0f9e-5dca-ba9f-d39c3d172355" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81e3b89d-a932-5551-882e-cf97243e80bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-333129" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3{e}^{1\\cdot t}+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t}+1 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2fe2a56-87fa-54f1-8bda-525eba574bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t}+2e^{3t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2fe2a56-87fa-54f1-8bda-525eba574bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t}+2e^{3t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434020} :answer-field/id #uuid "d27e42ca-cf51-537c-93bc-c24a5d179100" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a22272d0-9fb6-5234-800e-83cf913bd389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a22272d0-9fb6-5234-800e-83cf913bd389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434013} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a0fa9d7-a6e9-5102-9558-03b18008e8b7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-